<section xml:id="sec-ch03-06-CriticalPoints" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">

  <title>Critical Points and Analysis</title>

  <note>
    <p>Recall from Calculus I:</p>

    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>
            A function <m>f(x)</m> has a local maximum at <m>x=a</m> if
            <m>f(a) \geq f(x)</m> for all <m>x</m> in some interval
            <m>(a-h, a+h), h \gt 0</m>.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <p>
            A function <m>f(x)</m> has a local minimum at <m>x=b</m> if
            <m>f(b) \leq f(x)</m> for all <m>x</m> in some interval
            <m>(b-h, b+h), h \gt 0</m>.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </p>
  </note>

  <figure xml:id="fig-ch03-06-local-min-max">
    <caption>A function with a local minimum on the left, with a local maximum on the right.</caption>

    <sidebyside widths="45% 45%" margins="auto" valign="middle">
